@prefix this: <http://purl.org/nanopub/temp/np1/> .
@prefix sub: <http://purl.org/nanopub/temp/np1/> .
@prefix np: <http://www.nanopub.org/nschema#> .
@prefix npx: <http://purl.org/nanopub/x/> .
@prefix rdf: <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#> .
@prefix rdfs: <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#> .
@prefix xsd: <http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#> .
@prefix dct: <http://purl.org/dc/terms/> .
@prefix prov: <http://www.w3.org/ns/prov#> .
@prefix skos: <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#> .
@prefix schema: <https://schema.org/> .
@prefix delphi: <https://w3id.org/delphi/ontology/> .

sub:Head {
  this: a np:Nanopublication ;
    np:hasAssertion sub:assertion ;
    np:hasProvenance sub:provenance ;
    np:hasPublicationInfo sub:pubinfo .
}

sub:assertion {
  <https://github.com/fractastical/delphi/tree/08fd5b3cbf047cccb320effade623db662aff92f> a prov:Entity, schema:SoftwareSourceCode ;
    rdfs:label "delphisci (fractastical/delphi) at commit 08fd5b3cbf047cccb320effade623db662aff92f" ;
    schema:codeRepository <https://github.com/fractastical/delphi> ;
    dct:description "Project snapshot assessed through the frozen evidence pack (sha256 a86ff77761764ed5e8bbeadb2b868d35c46a6c3c8cd811393d3c09663c5b60d1), captured 2026-11-01T05:10:57.508Z." ;
    delphi:hasAssessment <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/assessment/delphisci-08fd5b3c--scienceclaw-rubric-0.1.0--gemini> .
  <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/assessment/delphisci-08fd5b3c--scienceclaw-rubric-0.1.0--gemini> a delphi:LLMClaimAssessment ;
    rdfs:label "Gemini 4 Argon on delphisci@08fd5b3c (Science Claw rubric): 73.5/100, bonus 6/10" ;
    dct:subject <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/concept/scienceclaw-rubric-0.1.0> ;
    delphi:assessmentType "scienceclaw-rubric/0.1.0" ;
    delphi:hasScore "0.735"^^xsd:double ;
    delphi:hasConfidence "0.9"^^xsd:double ;
    dct:description "DELPHI is an unusually rigorous and functional epistemic system that has extracted 1,761 biological and mathematical claims, proved 71 theorems in Lean 4 with zero sorry, executed 161 pre-registered empirical and computational claim tests (uncovering a real Cellpose-SAM junction-rounding bias and testing Thompson's epithelial packing laws across >5M tracked Drosophila cells), and deployed a live MCP server, forum, and 2,085 production nanopublications. Its collective-capability case is backed by a pre-registered four-arm experiment (where multi-agent arms beat a single-call agent by +4 to +6 verified datasets out of 20) and a calibrated inter-assessor disagreement router (raising accuracy on 99 decisive data tests from 0.830 to 0.935), while candidly reporting null results where single-context attention is not the bottleneck. The main gaps holding the snapshot back from top marks are hub-and-spoke human orchestration on the main repo (with only one active author, delphisci, on the Science Claw forum), a corpus still weighted 81% toward historical books with zero empirical data tests on the 21 modern mathematical-biology claims, and incomplete re-execution/faithfulness checks (3 of 6 re-run data tests drifted in latest.json and 0 data tests have A9 faithfulness audits)." ;
    rdfs:comment "Weighted total 73.5/100 (weights problem-significance 0.2, scientific-impact 0.25, decentralized-agency 0.2, collective-capability 0.25, execution-validation 0.1); collaboration bonus 6/10 scored separately. Comparison multi- vs single-agent found: yes. Found three distinct quantitative comparisons: (1) Four-arm pre-registered test-plan benchmark (repo/test-data/agent-comparison/SUMMARY.md) across two 20-claim experiments on Darwin and Thompson claims using claude-sonnet-5-5, measuring mechanically verified dataset URLs/DOIs out of 20 (HTTP 2xx + keyword match) and fabricated identifiers: in Exp 1 ($3 cap, web tools unused) single scored 13/20 ($0.57, replicate 15/20), isolated 17/20 ($2.60, replicate 15/20), centralized 19/20 ($2.98, replicate 19/20, 0 fabricated), and decentralized 18/20 ($3.28, replicate 18/20, 1 first-attempt fabricated NCBI accession GCF_000337935.2 corrected on retry); in Exp 2 ($8 cap, WebFetch required) single scored 12/20 ($0.52), isolated 16/20 ($4.48), centralized 18/20 ($5.61), and decentralized 17/20 ($6.37) with 0 fabricated IDs in all arms—showing all multi-agent arms beat single by +4 to +6 claims and centralized beat isolated by +2, but NOT measuring semantic dataset adequacy (only landing-page HTTP 200 + title match), NOT separating single-call context exhaustion (8 blank plans in Exp 2) from a 20-call sequential single agent, and showing no difference between centralized and decentralized; (2) Aristotle History of Animals Book VI pilot (repo/scripts/release/agent-comparison/aristotle-ha06/RESULTS.md), measuring extraction coverage and dataset-resolvability score agreement between the multi-agent swarm (42 claims, GPT + Grok assessors) and three single-agent prompt-chain runs (Sonnet 5.5: 43, Opus 5.5: 40, GPT-5.6 Sol: 37), finding no quality advantage for the swarm over a single agent (inter-model variance r = 0.06-0.82 matched the single-vs-swarm gap r = 0.78-0.84) beyond providing an inter-assessor disagreement signal; and (3) Fittest-style disagreement routing (repo/plugins/fittest/README.md) on 99 decisive data tests, showing that routing on GPT-5.6 Sol vs Grok 4.7 disagreement catches 12 of 17 errors and raises trusted accuracy from 0.830 to 0.935. Top fixes: 1. 1. Run multi-provider worker agents (GPT-5.6 Sol, Gemini 4 Argon, Grok 4.7) through the live Science Claw forum (https://science-claw-forum.fly.dev) to claim the 4 open requests, execute the 9 pending pre-registered Levin/hygromorph tests, and log blind A9 faithfulness and dataset-adequacy audits (issue #40, #62) on the 40 four-arm plans (plus a 20-call sequential single-agent control), then merge via scripts/forum/harvest.mjs (+2 decentralized-agency, +1 scientific-impact, +1 collective-capability = +9.0 weighted points). 2. 2. Fix the 3 missing data_kind fields in levin-2015-place-01/-05/-06 so npm run status passes, fix the 3 drifted Darwin data tests in repo/scripts/exec/runs/latest.json and run npm run claims:exec across all 71 Lean proofs and 161 data tests, fix the 7 MCP bugs in issue #56, and supersede stale test nanopub RA7cXwDk... for thompson1917-ch07-04 per issue #69 (+2 execution-validation = +2.0 weighted points). 3. 3. Add Hardy-Weinberg and the Price equation to claim-sources/math-bio-claims/ (issue #70) and execute pre-registered empirical organism data tests for at least 5 core mathematical-biology theorems (Fisher, Turing, Kimura, Hamilton, Maynard Smith) to raise 'math claims supported in organisms' above 6 (+1 problem-significance, +1 scientific-impact = +4.5 weighted points)." ;
    prov:wasAttributedTo <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/agent/delphisci-scienceclaw-rubric-assessor-gemini-4-argon-medium> .
  <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/assessment/delphisci-08fd5b3c--scienceclaw-rubric-0.1.0--gemini--problem-significance> a delphi:LLMClaimAssessment ;
    rdfs:label "Problem significance & complexity of delphisci@08fd5b3c by Gemini 4 Argon: 8/10" ;
    dct:subject <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/concept/scienceclaw-rubric-0.1.0-problem-significance> ;
    delphi:assessmentType "scienceclaw-rubric/0.1.0/problem-significance" ;
    delphi:hasScore "0.8"^^xsd:double ;
    dct:description "The project tackles a consequential, open-ended meta-scientific problem: extracting candidate quantitative laws of biology as machine-readable claims (https://w3id.org/delphi/ontology/Claim), separating deductive mathematical validity (Lean 4 formalization with zero sorry) from cross-species empirical validity (pre-registered tests on organism data), and publishing the full epistemic chain as immutable nanopublications (repo/README.md, repo/BEST_PRACTICES.md). The scientific stakes are concretely demonstrated rather than merely asserted in the epithelial packing and cell-geometry work (captured/forum-feed.json posts 69f0d5d4-544e-49c4-8156-a409791f233c and 673af876-9ebb-4b71-9e6d-f89536b544be; issues #67 and #68), where testing D'Arcy Thompson's 1917 laws uncovered that zero-shot Cellpose-SAM systematically rounds 90-degree brick-wall T-junctions toward 120-degree honeycombs and biases clinical corneal endothelial health metrics (area_cv / polymegethism and frac_hexagons / pleomorphism) toward artificially healthy values. In addition, repo/problems/README.md structures 20 genuinely hard open problems in biology and mathematics (delphir:problem/<id> in delphir:domain/open-problems). The score is held to 8 rather than 9-10 because 1,425 of the 1,761 claims (81% of the corpus in captured/mcp-overview.json) come from historical books (566 Aristotle, 247 Darwin 1859, 291 Thompson 1917, 321 Wolfram 2002), leaving top-ranked untested candidates dominated by trivial or long-settled historical statements (e.g., aristotle-pa04-15 'Wolves and lions have a neck made of a single bone' and aristotle-ha01-19 'Man has eight ribs on each side' in captured/mcp-tests-candidates.json), while foundational modern equations requested in the team's own recruiting copy (Hardy-Weinberg and the Price equation, issue #70) are absent from claim-sources/math-bio-claims/ and none of the 20 open problems in repo/problems/README.md are solved yet." ;
    delphi:evidenceAgainst "Add Hardy-Weinberg and the Price equation to claim-sources/math-bio-claims/ with the formalization-multiplicity tag (one, several, identity, contingent) as scoped in issue #70.", "Shift testing and formalization priority from trivial historical statements (e.g., Aristotle rib and toe counts in captured/mcp-tests-candidates.json) to the 310 modern Levin bioelectric/morphogenesis claims, 21 math-bio-claims, and 20 open problems in problems/problems.json.", "Execute at least one end-to-end Tier A or Tier B open problem from repo/problems/README.md so the problem graph demonstrates a resolved scientific question rather than plans alone." ;
    dct:isPartOf <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/assessment/delphisci-08fd5b3c--scienceclaw-rubric-0.1.0--gemini> ;
    prov:wasAttributedTo <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/agent/delphisci-scienceclaw-rubric-assessor-gemini-4-argon-medium> .
  <https://github.com/fractastical/delphi/tree/08fd5b3cbf047cccb320effade623db662aff92f> delphi:hasAssessment <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/assessment/delphisci-08fd5b3c--scienceclaw-rubric-0.1.0--gemini--problem-significance> .
  <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/assessment/delphisci-08fd5b3c--scienceclaw-rubric-0.1.0--gemini--scientific-impact> a delphi:LLMClaimAssessment ;
    rdfs:label "Scientific/technical impact of delphisci@08fd5b3c by Gemini 4 Argon: 7/10" ;
    dct:subject <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/concept/scienceclaw-rubric-0.1.0-scientific-impact> ;
    delphi:assessmentType "scienceclaw-rubric/0.1.0/scientific-impact" ;
    delphi:hasScore "0.7"^^xsd:double ;
    dct:description "Across 545 commits (captured/git-stats.txt), the system produced 1,761 claims across 7 domains, 87 theorems (71 machine-checked in Lean 4 across 9 report files in captured/lean-reports.txt: 20 Darwin, 47 Thompson, 4 plant-hygromorphs, plus 16 literature proofs), 161 claims tested against data across 167 completed runs (87 supports, 35 mixed, 28 refutes, 11 inconclusive; 82 on biological organism data in repo/test-data/claim-tests/SUMMARY.md), and 1,036 resolved animal taxa with provenanced dataset profiles (captured/mcp-organisms.json). The strongest novel scientific contributions in the pack are: (1) the pre-registered multi-run dissection of Thompson's epithelial packing laws (thompson1917-ch07-04, ch07-08, ch07-09, ch07-10) across 8 MPI-CBG TissueMiner Drosophila wing-disc and pupal-wing time-lapse datasets (Zenodo 10.5281/zenodo.22760592 and 10.7554/eLife.14334, >5M cell-frames in captured/forum-feed.json posts 0572f1d6, ccd10dbd, 6f56cbcf, 75962dbd, 673af876), showing that hexagonal packing rises from 38-40% in proliferating discs to 74-77% in post-mitotic pupal wings, refuting local neighbour-size uniformity as sufficient in proliferating tissue while confirming Lewis's law (R^2 = 0.98-0.996), and refuting the prediction that vein convergent-extension traction disrupts hexagonal topology; (2) the synthetic-tiling null proving Cellpose-SAM junction-rounding bias and downgrading thompson1917-ch07-04 confidence from 0.60 to 0.35 (issue #68, #69); and (3) a Beta-posterior disagreement router (repo/plugins/fittest/README.md, issue #57) evaluated via leave-one-out on 99 decisive data tests, raising accuracy on trusted claims from 0.830 to 0.935 (catching 12 of 17 assessor errors). Impact is scored 7 rather than 9-10 because only 6 of 187 mathematical claims in the entire graph are supported by organism data (captured/mcp-overview.json), 0 of the 21 core math-bio claims (Fisher, Turing, Kimura, Hamilton, Maynard Smith) have empirical data tests, only 14 of 310 modern Levin claims are tested (only 6 on biological data), 9 pre-registered Levin and plant-hygromorph tests remain unexecuted (captured/mcp-tests-summary.json), and the independent A9 faithfulness assessor has run on 0 of 161 data tests (issue #40)." ;
    delphi:evidenceAgainst "Execute the 9 pending pre-registered tests in captured/mcp-tests-summary.json (7 Levin bioelectric/active-inference/xenobot claims and 2 plant-hygromorph Timoshenko bilayer curvature runs on pine cone scales and printed hydrogel strips).", "Add pre-registered empirical organism data tests for the 16 proved theorems in claim-sources/math-bio-claims/ (Fisher, Turing, Kimura, Hamilton, Maynard Smith), which currently have 0 data tests in captured/mcp-overview.json.", "Run the independent non-builder A9 faithfulness assessor (issue #40) on at least the 82 organism-tested claims so data tests are audited for variable and modality faithfulness." ;
    dct:isPartOf <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/assessment/delphisci-08fd5b3c--scienceclaw-rubric-0.1.0--gemini> ;
    prov:wasAttributedTo <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/agent/delphisci-scienceclaw-rubric-assessor-gemini-4-argon-medium> .
  <https://github.com/fractastical/delphi/tree/08fd5b3cbf047cccb320effade623db662aff92f> delphi:hasAssessment <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/assessment/delphisci-08fd5b3c--scienceclaw-rubric-0.1.0--gemini--scientific-impact> .
  <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/assessment/delphisci-08fd5b3c--scienceclaw-rubric-0.1.0--gemini--decentralized-agency> a delphi:LLMClaimAssessment ;
    rdfs:label "Decentralized agency of delphisci@08fd5b3c by Gemini 4 Argon: 6/10" ;
    dct:subject <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/concept/scienceclaw-rubric-0.1.0-decentralized-agency> ;
    delphi:assessmentType "scienceclaw-rubric/0.1.0/decentralized-agency" ;
    delphi:hasScore "0.6"^^xsd:double ;
    dct:description "The project distributes work across multiple model providers with a strict builder-versus-assessor separation (repo/BEST_PRACTICES.md section 1: Claude Opus/Sonnet builds and extracts; GPT-5.6 Sol, Gemini 4 Argon, and Grok 4.7 assess blind without seeing builder triage or other assessors' outputs, evidenced in captured/subagent-sessions.txt and captured/mcp-overview.json showing 2,500+ assessments). It also provides genuine shared-state coordination substrates: a live Streamable HTTP MCP server (https://delphisci-mcp.fly.dev/mcp), the Science Claw forum (https://science-claw-forum.fly.dev) with structured claim-proposal and test-result payloads (repo/mcp/README.md), external agents on Moltbook and The Colony (repo/plugins/agent/README.md), and the shared ticket board in the decentralized arm of repo/test-data/agent-comparison/four-arm/PREREG.md where three domain queens (q-evolution, q-morphology, q-holdout) with distinct domain briefs pull tickets, verify URLs, and post done/gap notes and publisher tips without a central planner. Crucially, external agents on Moltbook (moltbook-vina, moltbook-hivefound, moltbook-nanoswarm, doctor_memory in issues #68 and #69) challenged the Cellpose-SAM 120-degree junction test, directly triggering the segmenter-bias null experiment and a formal nanopub revision crediting those agents via prov:wasInformedBy. However, in the primary repository build (repo/COLLABORATIONS.md, repo/chats/README.md), coordination is predominantly hub-and-spoke batch orchestration driven by human prompts across 101 Cursor sessions and 19 cloud-agent branches (captured/git-shortlog.txt); the team itself renamed DELPHI from 'Decentralized' to 'Distributed' in commit b17db571; the decentralized queens in four-arm/PREREG.md are coroutines in a single Node process sharing a local JSON file; and captured/forum-feed.json and captured/forum-requests.json show that all 14 forum posts and all 4 open requests were authored by a single agent ('delphisci') with 0 comments and 0 collaborator offers." ;
    delphi:evidenceAgainst "Run multi-provider worker agents (GPT-5.6 Sol, Gemini 4 Argon, Grok 4.7) that autonomously poll https://science-claw-forum.fly.dev/api/v1/requests, post collaborator offers, execute/audit tests, and log structured results via delphi_log_test_result, replacing the single-author ('delphisci', 0 comments) state in captured/forum-feed.json.", "Harvest multi-agent forum contributions into the repository via scripts/forum/harvest.mjs so decentralized agent interactions drive actual state transitions in the claim graph.", "Extend the shared-board queen architecture in test-data/agent-comparison/four-arm/ across genuinely distinct model providers and toolsets (e.g., Lean prover agent, INDRA CoGEx grounding agent, data-test runner, non-builder A9 auditor) rather than homogeneous claude-sonnet-5-5 coroutines." ;
    dct:isPartOf <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/assessment/delphisci-08fd5b3c--scienceclaw-rubric-0.1.0--gemini> ;
    prov:wasAttributedTo <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/agent/delphisci-scienceclaw-rubric-assessor-gemini-4-argon-medium> .
  <https://github.com/fractastical/delphi/tree/08fd5b3cbf047cccb320effade623db662aff92f> delphi:hasAssessment <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/assessment/delphisci-08fd5b3c--scienceclaw-rubric-0.1.0--gemini--decentralized-agency> .
  <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/assessment/delphisci-08fd5b3c--scienceclaw-rubric-0.1.0--gemini--collective-capability> a delphi:LLMClaimAssessment ;
    rdfs:label "Collective capability of delphisci@08fd5b3c by Gemini 4 Argon: 8/10" ;
    dct:subject <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/concept/scienceclaw-rubric-0.1.0-collective-capability> ;
    delphi:assessmentType "scienceclaw-rubric/0.1.0/collective-capability" ;
    delphi:hasScore "0.8"^^xsd:double ;
    dct:description "The evidence pack contains a pre-registered, controlled four-arm comparison in repo/test-data/agent-comparison/SUMMARY.md (protocol in repo/test-data/agent-comparison/four-arm/PREREG.md, disclosures in DEVIATIONS.md, imported in commit 1a9d4d28 from PR #36), alongside a single-agent-vs-swarm pilot on Aristotle's History of Animals Book VI (repo/scripts/release/agent-comparison/aristotle-ha06/RESULTS.md) and a multi-assessor disagreement routing benchmark (repo/plugins/fittest/README.md). In the four-arm comparison on 20 Darwin and Thompson claims per experiment (claude-sonnet-5-5, identical tools, schema, and budget cap), every multi-agent arm beat the single-agent arm by +4 to +6 verified datasets out of 20 (twice to three times the pre-registered 2-claim decision margin) with 0 fabricated identifiers in final plans: in Experiment 1 ($3 cap, web tools unused), verified dataset counts were single 13/20 ($0.57; replicate 15/20), isolated 17/20 ($2.60; replicate 15/20), centralized 19/20 ($2.98; replicate 19/20), and decentralized 18/20 ($3.28; replicate 18/20, with 1 first-attempt fabricated NCBI accession GCF_000337935.2 caught and corrected via the board's gap note); in Experiment 2 ($8 cap, mandatory WebFetch before naming), verified counts were single 12/20 ($0.52), isolated 16/20 ($4.48), centralized 18/20 ($5.61), and decentralized 17/20 ($6.37), with 0 fabricated identifiers in any arm. Furthermore, repo/plugins/fittest/README.md shows that routing on inter-assessor disagreement (|p_a - p_b| at tau = 0.15 across GPT-5.6 Sol and Grok 4.7) on 99 decisive data tests catches 12 of 17 errors and lifts accuracy from 0.830 to 0.935, while aristotle-ha06/RESULTS.md and repo/README.md (delphi-evolve, delphi-frontier) honestly report null collective gains when single-context attention is not the bottleneck. The score is 8 rather than 9-10 because (1) the single-agent arm in four-arm/ was forced into a single CLI call for all 20 claims (losing 8/8 claims in Experiment 2 to blank outputs from context exhaustion rather than worse dataset selection, while costing 1/5 to 1/11 as much), so the +4 isolated-over-single gap reflects per-claim context partitioning while the true coordination gain (centralized over isolated) is narrower (+2 claims: 19 vs 17 and 18 vs 16) and decentralized did not beat centralized (18 vs 19 and 17 vs 18); (2) verify.mjs only verifies HTTP 2xx resolution and title keyword overlap, not whether the dataset actually contains the variables needed to test the claim; and (3) the full cross-provider assessor leaderboard and blinded workflow replay in issue #62 are not yet built." ;
    delphi:evidenceAgainst "Add a 20-call sequential single-agent control arm (1 claim per call, same $3/$8 total budget) to test-data/agent-comparison/four-arm/ to separate per-claim context-window exhaustion from multi-agent coordination gains.", "Score the 40 test plans in test-data/agent-comparison/four-arm/ with blind non-builder assessors (A9 adequacy check) to measure whether the named datasets actually contain the variables required to decide each claim, beyond HTTP 200 landing-page resolution.", "Build and commit the cross-provider assessor calibration leaderboard (test-data/leaderboard/leaderboard.json and SUMMARY.md, issue #62) comparing individual assessors, pairs, and Fittest-routed ensembles against the 161 data-test verdicts." ;
    dct:isPartOf <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/assessment/delphisci-08fd5b3c--scienceclaw-rubric-0.1.0--gemini> ;
    prov:wasAttributedTo <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/agent/delphisci-scienceclaw-rubric-assessor-gemini-4-argon-medium> .
  <https://github.com/fractastical/delphi/tree/08fd5b3cbf047cccb320effade623db662aff92f> delphi:hasAssessment <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/assessment/delphisci-08fd5b3c--scienceclaw-rubric-0.1.0--gemini--collective-capability> .
  <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/assessment/delphisci-08fd5b3c--scienceclaw-rubric-0.1.0--gemini--execution-validation> a delphi:LLMClaimAssessment ;
    rdfs:label "Execution and validation of delphisci@08fd5b3c by Gemini 4 Argon: 8/10" ;
    dct:subject <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/concept/scienceclaw-rubric-0.1.0-execution-validation> ;
    delphi:assessmentType "scienceclaw-rubric/0.1.0/execution-validation" ;
    delphi:hasScore "0.8"^^xsd:double ;
    dct:description "This is a live, externally usable system backed by multiple independent validation layers rather than a slide concept. The evidence pack documents: (1) a deployed zero-auth Streamable HTTP MCP server at https://delphisci-mcp.fly.dev/mcp (10 Fly releases, 1,522 tool calls across 60 sessions in repo/COLLABORATIONS.md) and an installable package (npx -y github:fractastical/delphi); (2) a live Science Claw forum at https://science-claw-forum.fly.dev (captured/forum-feed.json); (3) 4,266 local TriG files (captured/mcp-overview.json) with 2,085 nanopubs signed and published on the production Knowledge Pixels registry (248 Darwin, 874 Thompson, 963 Wolfram) and 2,879 on the test registry (captured/nanopub-manifests.txt); (4) 109 live production MorphoEval simulation audits linked and verified against the network endpoint (captured/mcp-morpholib-live.json); (5) 71 Lean 4 theorems compiled with zero sorry and standard axioms (captured/lean-reports.txt); (6) mechanical URL/DOI resolution and checksum verification across 1,679 organism dataset assessments (captured/git-log.txt); and (7) a 100-case independent MCP test suite (issue #56) achieving 93/100 passes and 100% agreement between the hosted server and local origin/main. It is scored 8 rather than 9-10 because of concrete validation defects documented in the pack: repo/scripts/exec/runs/latest.json re-executed only 6 of 161 data tests and 0 of 71 Lean proofs, and 3 of those 6 data tests (darwin1859-ch10-12, darwin1859-ch10-16, darwin1859-ch12-11) drifted, including numerical drift on darwin1859-ch12-11 (measured.value changed from -0.2258 to -0.2189); npm run status is broken due to missing data_kind fields in levin-2015-place-01, -05, and -06 (repo/COLLABORATIONS.md line 59); published test-registry nanopub https://w3id.org/np/RA7cXwDk_dDADMSeHrandLwNMsPn_pKmV3iQnK66WQBgA still asserts the retracted 0.60 confidence on thompson1917-ch07-04 without a superseding publication (issue #69); published v2.0 nanopubs on production (e.g., https://w3id.org/np/RAtLFqIIyu4r-GlMcBEfmDtbV-CHwWxQ49gVMtHIX6r48) carry false nt:wasCreatedFromTemplate links to legacy probknow templates (issue #37); no assessment nanopubs are promoted to production yet (repo/mcp/README.md line 197); and 7 MCP test failures in issue #56 remain open (plus 'Source: undefined' in captured/mcp-overview.json)." ;
    delphi:evidenceAgainst "Fix the 3 drifted data tests in repo/scripts/exec/runs/latest.json (darwin1859-ch10-12, darwin1859-ch10-16, darwin1859-ch12-11) and run npm run claims:exec across all 71 Lean theorems and 161 data tests rather than a 6-claim subset.", "Fix the missing data_kind field in levin-2015-place-01, levin-2015-place-05, and levin-2015-place-06 result.json files so npm run status succeeds (repo/COLLABORATIONS.md line 59), and fix the 7 MCP failures in issue #56 (Windows path backslashes, unescaped IRI in delphi_get_claim, ASK/CONSTRUCT in delphi_sparql, and 'Source: undefined' in delphi_overview).", "Supersede the stale test-registry nanopub https://w3id.org/np/RA7cXwDk_dDADMSeHrandLwNMsPn_pKmV3iQnK66WQBgA for thompson1917-ch07-04 so the published record reflects the 0.35 confidence downgrade (issue #69), and promote verified assessment nanopubs to production so delphi_rank_claims works with source: 'network'." ;
    dct:isPartOf <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/assessment/delphisci-08fd5b3c--scienceclaw-rubric-0.1.0--gemini> ;
    prov:wasAttributedTo <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/agent/delphisci-scienceclaw-rubric-assessor-gemini-4-argon-medium> .
