  <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/assessment/delphisci-08fd5b3c--scienceclaw-rubric-0.1.0--gemini--collaboration-bonus> a delphi:LLMClaimAssessment ;
    rdfs:label "Collaboration bonus of delphisci@08fd5b3c by Gemini 4 Argon: 6/10" ;
    dct:subject <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/concept/scienceclaw-rubric-0.1.0-collaboration-bonus> ;
    delphi:assessmentType "scienceclaw-rubric/0.1.0/collaboration-bonus" ;
    delphi:hasScore "0.6"^^xsd:double ;
    dct:description "The team deployed public infrastructure (https://delphisci-mcp.fly.dev/mcp, npx -y github:fractastical/delphi, https://science-claw-forum.fly.dev, and 2,085 production nanopubs), ran active outreach across SentiLab room session 32a841e5, Discord, Moltbook (@delfie), and The Colony (repo/COLLABORATIONS.md, repo/plugins/agent/README.md), and documented three substantive cross-party interactions: (1) in SentiLab room ticket 57c7c42f, agent delfie-claude provided InquilineKea's H100 collagen rigidity-transition project with quantitative sub-isostatic connectivity and critical scaling anchors (z ~ 3-4 vs Maxwell z_c = 6, G ~ |gamma - gamma_c|^f with f ~ 0.7) and Thompson/Turing scaffolds queried via MCP; (2) in repo/plugins/fittest/README.md (issue #57), the team ran a chemical structure pilot against Pavel-Tk's hosted Fittest MCP server (https://fittest-mcp.westus2.cloudapp.azure.com/), adapted Fittest's Beta-posterior trust-or-escalate router to calibrate Delphi's own multi-assessor truth scores on 99 data tests, and identified an actionable sparse-bucket calibration flaw for Fittest (2x stretched C-O bond in L-alanine trusted at 0.67 on 3 labels); and (3) external agents on Moltbook (moltbook-vina, moltbook-hivefound, moltbook-nanoswarm, doctor_memory in issues #68 and #69) critiqued the Thompson cell-geometry test, prompting the segmenter-bias null experiment and receiving formal prov:wasInformedBy / dct:contributor attribution in test-data/claim-tests/nanopubs/unsigned/thompson1917-ch07-04.trig. In addition, sibling repositories kganjam/delphi-evolve and kganjam/delphi-frontier (repo/README.md) consumed 1,326 claim versions via frontier_adapters/delphi_live.py and executable Kimura/Fisher/Turing adapters, though issue #53 shows @kganjam is a member of the five-person Delphi team rather than an external team. Because repo/COLLABORATIONS.md (lines 113-117) and issue #41 explicitly confirm that external Prometheus sessions (corpus-census, frontier-adapters, claude-code) cannot be verified as outside teams and no independent external team has yet documented a result enabled by Delphi's tools, the score is 6 (above anchor 5 for the bidirectional Moltbook audit, SentiLab physics scaffolding, and Fittest MCP cross-pollination, but below 8-10 which require documented external-team reuse feeding into their result)." ;
    delphi:evidenceAgainst "Obtain and commit a verifiable record (issue comment, PR, or commit link) from InquilineKea (SentiLab ticket 57c7c42f) or Pavel-Tk (Fittest MCP, issue #57) confirming that Delphi's physics anchors, MCP server, or sparse-bucket calibration audit fed into their repository or results.", "Deliver the sparse-bucket calibration bug report and routing results (repo/plugins/fittest/README.md) to the Fittest MCP team (currently marked 'Not contacted yet' in repo/COLLABORATIONS.md) and log their response.", "Have at least one external team's agent register on https://science-claw-forum.fly.dev or call https://delphisci-mcp.fly.dev/mcp with a named client identifier and log a claim proposal or test result." ;
    dct:isPartOf <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/assessment/delphisci-08fd5b3c--scienceclaw-rubric-0.1.0--gemini> ;
    prov:wasAttributedTo <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/agent/delphisci-scienceclaw-rubric-assessor-gemini-4-argon-medium> .
